cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "TEagle: an evidence-traceable integrated single-locus workflow for transposable-element classification and PCR assay planning"
abstract: >-
  TEagle is a native Windows desktop application that integrates established methods for single-locus transposable-element structural detection, domain-based classification, PCR assay planning, in-silico screening, and sealed provenance. It withholds classifications when the available evidence does not support a call. Protocol 2.3.6 results are version-locked to TEagle 3.9.0. The TEagle 4.0.0 prospective benchmark is a separate public record (see references) and applies only to that release. No evaluation result establishes population-level accuracy or prospective wet-lab performance, or carries over to a later release.
version: 4.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-26
license: AGPL-3.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/tunabirgun/TEagle"
